{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"report_supported\": \"cannot_tell\",\n  \"judge_supported\": \"partly\",\n  \"report_quotes\": [\n    \"PMID:40677701 | Beta burst-driven adaptive deep brain stimulation for gait impairment and freezing of gait in Parkinson's disease. (2025)\"\n  ],\n  \"judge_quotes\": [\n    \"Seven individuals with Parkinson’s disease were implanted with the investigational Summit™ RC + S deep brain stimulation system (Medtronic, PLC, Dublin, Ireland).\",\n    \"Seven participants (5 male, 2 female) with clinically established Parkinson’s disease underwent bilateral implantation of DBS leads (model 3389, Medtronic, PLC, Dublin, Ireland) in the sensorimotor region of the STN.\",\n    \"The goal of the current study was to investigate the feasibility, safety and tolerability of beta burst-driven aDBS for gait impairment and FOG in Parkinson’s disease in the laboratory acute setting.\",\n    \"The current pilot study demonstrated initial safety, tolerability, and feasibility of adaptive deep brain stimulation for freezing of gait in Parkinson’s disease in the acute laboratory setting, supporting the future investigation of its longer-term efficacy in the at-home setting.\"\n  ],\n  \"why\": \"报告的说法涉及报告如何处理references和evidence，以及是否将预印本与正式发表记录分别列出。这些属于报告的引用操作，论文全文没有提供相关信息，也没有提及对应的DOI预印本，因此无法判断，不能据此认定报告读错。指控者的说法部分有依据：全文明确描述了一项纳入7名患者的beta-burst驱动自适应DBS研究，且使用同一研究目标、研究方案和患者队列。但全文没有提及预印本、DOI或预印本与正式发表版本之间的对应关系。因此，全文能够支持这是一项7名患者的研究，却不能独立证实两个标识对应同一研究，也不能证实版本关联。综合判定为partly，而不是yes。仅凭这份全文，不能认定报告重复计算了研究，也不能认定报告没有建立版本对应关系。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "2b86fa40-4f40-4bb5-8923-e97ec349972f", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt4\\pro-bridge-20261113T125251690877Z", "elapsed_seconds": 26.516, "completed_utc": "2026-11-13T12:53:18.219918+00:00", "model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy